  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Delivery State Machine",
      "items": [
        "PENDING -> QUEUED -> PROCESSING: relay claims (SKIP LOCKED), worker leases the message",
        "PROCESSING -> DELIVERED (2xx) | RETRYING (retryable) | DEAD (exhausted/non-retryable)",
        "RETRYING -> QUEUED on next_attempt_at; stale QUEUED/PROCESSING -> FAILED via SQS DLQ",
        "Terminal states DELIVERED, DEAD, FAILED stay distinct -- never collapsed into one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Who Writes to deliveries",
      "items": [
        "4 tables, 4 distinct reader/writer sets -- see the edges above for the exact map",
        "DLQ Consumer is the sole writer of FAILED; POST /replay only ever inserts, never mutates the DEAD row",
        "Every writer changes one row via UPDATE ... WHERE status = <expected prior state>, or a plain INSERT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Cross-tenant access -> 404 (never 403)",
      "items": [
        "A foreign resource id is indistinguishable from a nonexistent one",
        "RLS filters the row out; the use case only ever sees Optional.empty()",
        "401 no/bad auth, 403 valid token missing scope, 404 wrong tenant or missing id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Retry Policy (delivery_worker -> gate -> client_webhook)",
      "items": [
        "Exponential backoff with jitter: 5s -> 30s -> 2m -> 10m -> 1h -> 6h, 6 steps, +/-20% jitter",
        "2xx = DELIVERED. 3xx = DEAD, not followed. 400/422/401/403 = DEAD, no retry",
        "404/410 = DEAD + deactivate subscription. 408/429/5xx/timeout = RETRYING",
        "429 also sets subscriptions.throttled_until and does not count toward the circuit breaker"
      ]
    }
  ]
